1) Check Python 3.12 is available
py -0p
py -3.12 --version
If py -3.12 fails, install Python 3.12 first (from python.org), then retry.
2) Create the venv (from your project root)
cd C:\Users\viq021\repositories\Robot_Detective
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
3) Activate + upgrade packaging tools
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -V
python -m pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel
4) Install project dependencies
If you use setup.py:
python -m pip install -e .
Or if you have a requirements file:
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
5) Make it show as library root in JetBrains
In JetBrains (PyCharm/JetBrains-PY):
File -> Settings -> Project -> Python Interpreter
Click gear icon -> Add...
Choose Existing environment
Select:
C:\Users\viq021\repositories\Robot_Detective\.venv\Scripts\python.exe
Apply/OK
After this, .venv\Lib\site-packages appears under External Libraries (that’s the interpreter library root).
6) If it still doesn’t appear
Use File -> Invalidate Caches / Restart
Re-open interpreter settings and confirm it points to .venv\Scripts\python.exe
In terminal, confirm pip path:
python -m pip -V
It should point inside .venv.
